course: dictionary
lesson: 7585
title: Prefixes: pre- means before
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a few letters added to the front of a word that change its meaning. Pre- means before. You already know view means to look at, so a preview is looking at something before everyone else can.
explain: Read «a sneak preview» and ask what the word sneak tells you. It suggests a secret look early, before the main showing. Try your meaning in the phrase: "a secret look before the main showing" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Preview works as a noun (a preview) and a verb (to preview). «Let's preview the chapter» means look at the headings and pictures first. Previewing a book helps you predict what it is about and understand it better.
fact: Pre- is a prefix that means before.
fact: Preview is made from pre- (before) and view (to look at).
fact: «A preview» can be a trailer, which is a short look at something coming later.
fact: «Print preview» shows how a page will look before you print it.
fact: Previewing a book means looking at the cover, title and headings before you read.
exercise: «I saw a sneak preview of the film before it came out.» What does preview mean here? | A review written after the film | A ticket that costs less | A film that is shown again | *A chance to see something before everyone else
exercise: Which word has the prefix pre- meaning before? | redo | *preview | viewer | review
exercise: On a computer, «print preview» shows what? | The colour of the printer's ink | A list of your favourite files | How long the printer takes to work | *How a page will look before you print it
test: Before reading a book, Maya says, «I will preview the chapter first.» What will she do? | *Look at the title and headings before she reads | Read the last page to find out the ending | Ask a friend to read it aloud to her | Skip the book altogether
test: In the phrase «a short preview of the lesson», what does preview mean? | A snack eaten before lunch | A review of last week's work | *A short look at what the lesson will cover | A long test at the end of the lesson
exam: What does pre- mean in preview, and what does view mean? | *Pre- means before and view means to look at | Pre- means after and view means to hide | Pre- means again and view means to build | Pre- means under and view means to read
